--------------------Sure, here are the debug.assert statements corresponding to the comments starting with "@@@".

```cs
Debug.Assert(Old_arrListIndexOfX >= -1);
```
This assertion checks that the index of x in the old array list is greater than or equal to -1. In C#, the `IndexOf` method returns the zero-based index of the first occurrence of an item in the list, or -1 if item is not found. Therefore, the index of an item in the list should be greater than or equal to -1 for the item to be in the list.
--------------------Here are corresponding assertions that could be added at the end of each `PUT_` method:

```cs
Debug.Assert(Old_arrListCount < New_arrListCount, "Count not increased after add operation");
Debug.Assert(New_arrListIndexOfX == Old_arrListCount, "New element not added at the end");
Debug.Assert(New_Ret == Old_arrListCount, "Return value is not equal to new count");
Debug.Assert(New_arrListContainsX, "New element not found in collection after add operation");

Debug.Assert(New_arrListCount == Old_arrListCount - 1, "Count not decreased after remove operation");
Debug.Assert(New_arrListIndexOfX == -1, "Removed element still found in collection");
Debug.Assert(New_arrListContainsX == false, "Removed element still found in collection");

Debug.Assert(New_arrListCount == Old_arrListCount + 1, "Count not increased after insert operation");
Debug.Assert(New_arrListIndexOfX == index, "Inserted element not at correct position");
Debug.Assert(New_arrListContainsX, "Inserted element not found in collection after insert operation");

Debug.Assert(Old_arrList[index] == x, "Value at insert position should be old value");
Debug.Assert(New_arrList[index] == x, "Value at insert position should be new value");

Debug.Assert(New_Ret == arrList[index], "Get operation returned wrong value");
Debug.Assert(New_containsNewRet, "Get operation did not return added value");

Debug.Assert(Old_arrListContainsX == New_Ret, "Contains operation returned wrong value");

Debug.Assert(New_Ret == Old_arrListIndexOfX || New_Ret == -1, "IndexOf operation returned wrong index");
Debug.Assert(New_Ret == Old_arrListLastIndexOfX || New_Ret == -1, "LastIndexOf operation returned wrong index");

Debug.Assert(New_Ret == arrList.Count, "Count operation returned wrong value");
